// TEST: Floor Unit Carrying Complex (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3007
// ERROR-CONTAINS: floor is not defined for complex operands
// The other residue of units/076, and a MESSAGE pin as much as a refusal one.
// floor/ceil have no std::complex overload at any signature. Before the scalar
// arm looked through the unit wrapper, a `Complex128<volts>` operand missed the
// complex arm entirely and landed on the general one, which reported the
// SIGNATURE (BL3006, "volts is not dimensionless") -- true but beside the
// point, and it would have kept steering the author toward dividing by a
// reference quantity when no dimensionless complex would have helped either.
// Classifying on the stripped base names the real problem first.
Unit volts
let v: Float<volts> = 3.0
let z = complex(1.0, 2.0) * v
let bad = floor(z)
